# IntelliJ
# Covers JetBrains IDEs: IntelliJ, RubyMine, PhpStorm, AppCode, PyCharm, CLion, Android Studio and Webstorm
# Reference: https://intellij-support.jetbrains.com/hc/en-us/articles/206544839
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/master/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#
# Everything under .idea/ is ignored by default, because most of it is either user-specific
# (project SDK name, Gradle JVM, window layout, plugin state) or reconstructed from the Gradle
# model every time the project is imported. Tracking those files pushes one contributor's local
# IDE state onto everyone else, which breaks people who use a different JDK installation.
# The handful of files below are genuine shared project configuration, so they are re-included.
/.idea/*
!/.idea/.name
!/.idea/encodings.xml
!/.idea/inspectionProfiles/
!/.idea/runConfigurations/

# Only the run configurations that ship with the project are shared; the ones a contributor
# creates locally stay local.
/.idea/runConfigurations/*
!/.idea/runConfigurations/SwingStartup.xml
!/.idea/runConfigurations/openrocket_jar.xml
!/.idea/runConfigurations/openrocket_test.xml

# Module and project files (IntelliJ regenerates these from the Gradle import)
*.iml
**/*.iws

# Build output
**/out/
**/build/
**/.gradle**

# VSCode
.vscode/

# mpeltonen/sbt-idea plugin
**/.idea_modules/

# JIRA plugin
atlassian-ide-plugin.xml

# Crashlytics plugin (for Android Studio and IntelliJ)
com_crashlytics_export_strings.xml
crashlytics.properties
crashlytics-build.properties
fabric.properties

openrocket.log
**/hs_err_pid*.log

*.snap

# Sphinx documentation
docs/build

# AI tools
**/copilot.*.xml
**/AGENTS.md
**/CLAUDE.md
**/GEMINI.md
**/.claude

# Environment files
**/.env
